/*
==============================================================================
  PoC 03 -- the vacuity wellformedness checks are dead code
==============================================================================

  CLASS      : missing diagnostic.  NOT a wrong verdict -- see below.
  SEVERITY   : high -- Tamarin's only automatic guard against the most common
                       modelling error is unreachable
  AFFECTS    : tamarin-prover 1.12.0 and develop @ ef3f0468 (1.13.0)
  STATUS     : confirmed by the maintainers; fix proposed in PR #916 (open).

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  CORRECTION TO EARLIER VERSIONS OF THIS FILE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Earlier drafts classified this as a "missed attack" and listed
  `secrecy_typo: verified` as a wrong verdict.  That was an error.

  No rule emits `SecrettKey`, so `secrecy_typo` quantifies over an empty set
  and is VACUOUSLY TRUE.  `verified` is the correct answer to the question the
  lemma actually asks.  Tamarin's logic is right here.

  From the maintainers:

      "In theory 3, the property proven true is in fact true. But you are
       right that a warning should be generated to inform the user about the
       modeling mistake."

  The defect is that Tamarin ships a check for exactly this modelling error
  and the check never runs.  The user writes a lemma they believe says one
  thing, Tamarin proves a different and empty thing, and every diagnostic
  channel reports success.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ROOT CAUSE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lib/theory/src/Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:578-583

      -- | Report on facts usage. Skip checks on non-existant actions if
      -- `incompleteMSRs` is True.
      factReports incompleteMSRs thy =
          concat [ reservedReport, ..., factUsage, factLhsOccurNoRhs ]
          ++ concat [ inexistentActions ++ inexistentActionsRestrictions
                    | incompleteMSRs ]

  The list-comprehension guard is the INVERSE of its own docstring: it
  INCLUDES the checks when `incompleteMSRs` is True and skips them when it is
  False.  And the only production call site hardcodes False --
  src/Main/TheoryLoader.hs:602:

      incompleteMSRs = False
        -- TODO how do we know if we do not have all MSRs due to translation?

  Net effect: `inexistentActions` and `inexistentActionsRestrictions`
  (Wellformedness.hs:706-734) never execute in the shipped tool.  They are
  fully implemented, with error messages, and unreachable.

  Either reading condemns the code.  Under the docstring's intent the guard is
  backwards; under the guard's literal meaning the flag is set wrongly.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  REGRESSION PROVENANCE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
      git log -L 583,583:lib/theory/src/Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs

  pins the guard to commit 98c3887f, "Extend ProVerif export module (#725)".
  Before that PR both checks were unconditional members of `factReports`:

      factReports thy = concat
          [ reservedReport, reservedFactNameRules, freshFactArguments,
            specialFactsUsage, factUsage, factLhsOccurNoRhs,
            inexistentActions, inexistentActionsRestrictions ]

  An unrelated export-backend refactor disabled a working guardrail, and no
  test noticed, because the suite compares end-to-end verdicts on case studies
  and no case study depends on those checks firing.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  GROUND TRUTH
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  `secrecy_typo` is vacuously TRUE and Tamarin correctly reports it verified.
  `secrecy_intended` is FALSE and Tamarin correctly reports it falsified.
  Both verdicts are right.  The missing output is the warning.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  TAMARIN SAYS (1.12.0, unpatched)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    secrecy_typo     (all-traces): verified (2 steps)   <-- correct, and vacuous
    secrecy_intended (all-traces): falsified - found trace (3 steps)
    /* All wellformedness checks were successful. */

  `--quit-on-warning` does NOT help: no warning is produced at all, because
  the check that would produce it never runs.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  FIX
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  PR #916, which removes the `incompleteMSRs` flag entirely rather than
  inverting the guard, and resolves the TODO at TheoryLoader.hs:602.
==============================================================================
*/

theory VacuousLemmaTypo begin

rule Setup: [ Fr(k)   ] --[ SecretKey(k) ]-> [ Key(k) ]
rule Leak:  [ Key(k)  ] --[ Leaked(k)    ]-> [ Out(k) ]

// TYPO: the rules emit "SecretKey", this lemma says "SecrettKey".
// No rule has such an action, so the lemma is vacuously true. Tamarin's
// "verified" is correct; the missing output is a warning about the typo.
lemma secrecy_typo:
  "All k #i. SecrettKey(k) @ i ==> not(Ex #j. K(k) @ j)"

// The property that was actually intended. Correctly falsified.
lemma secrecy_intended:
  "All k #i. SecretKey(k) @ i ==> not(Ex #j. K(k) @ j)"

end
